From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:04:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: add the c2.v4l2.hevc.encoder component

The store offered AVC, VP8 and VP9 encoders only. Add an HEVC encoder that
the same property scheme enables, ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.encoder.supported.hevc.

The interface offers the profiles the device lists and its Main tier levels
(a default range when the device lists none), and checks a level against
the size, frame rate and bitrate with the HEVC level limits of Tables A.8
and A.9. The encoder sets the V4L2 HEVC profile, level and tier, no
B-frames, joined headers, and leaves the VPS, SPS and PPS to the device,
which writes them in front of each IDR; the AVC cache-and-inject path
stays AVC only. The codec-specific data is the VPS, SPS and PPS of the
first coded frame, and the frame rate ceiling follows the HEVC level.
